[[64,96,0,"<h3>Functional description</h3><p>The engine control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               monitors\nand controls the entire electronic injection system.</p><p>The supply for the engine control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is\ncontrolled by the ignition (15/54) at pin 58 by the line protected\nby fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F4</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of the additional fuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98A</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The relay \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>J10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               controls the  system\nsupply: it is supplied by the battery, from the line for maxifuse\nEFI of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B99</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ; pin 13 of the control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10 sends the enablement\nsignal which excites relay J10 and sends power to the control unit,\ndirectly to pin 5 and, via the line of fuse F3 of the additional\nfuse box B98A, to pin 4.</strong></p><p>The relay \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>J15</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is also supplied by\nthe battery, from the  line for maxifuse EFI of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B99</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ; pin\n24 of control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               sends the signals which energize the\nrelay \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>J15</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , which provides the supply to the fuel pump \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N40</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ,\nwhich is connected to earth through the inertia switch \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>I50</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .\nIn case of  impact, this cuts off the circuit to prevent the danger\nof fuel delivery. Pins 1, 2 and 3 of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               are earthed.</p><p>The diesel preheating relay \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>J17 is supplied\nby the battery via the line protected by the GLOW maxifuse of B99\nor fuse B39, and controls the operation of the diesel heating resistor\nO20;</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               a signal of the control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               (from pin 111)\ndeactivates the system once heating has taken place.</p><p>Control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M15</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , responsible for\ncontrolling preheating of heater plugs \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>A40</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , is supplied directly\nby the battery via a line protected by the GLOW maxifuse of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B99</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .\nIt is supplied - connector C - by the line of fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F2 of the\nadditional fuse box B98A, and exchanges the command and control\nsignals with pins 22 and 62 of M10 which controls the timer.</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               Connector\nB is connected to the heater plugs \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>A40.</strong></p><p>The engine control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               receives\nsignals from the various sensors in order to monitor all engine\nservice conditions.</p><p>The rpm sensor \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K46</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               provides information\nconcerning the engine speed through a frequency signal sent to pin\n100 of the control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              . It receives an earth signal\nfrom pin 99 of the control unit. Both signals are weak and are therefore suitably\nshielded by pin 101.</p><p>Timing sensor \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K47</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is supplied from\npin 102 of control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              . It receives a reference earth\nfrom pin 104 of the control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and sends a frequency signal\ncorresponding to the timing to pin 103.</p><p>The engine temperature sensor \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K36</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ,\nreceives a reference earth from pin 85 of the control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and\nsupplies a signal proportional to the temperature of the engine\ncoolant to pin 84.</p><p>The same sender unit also supplies information\nto the temperature gauge and warning light \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <a href=\"#/3234358\">E4023</a>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The air flow meter \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K41</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               receives a\ngeneral power supply from the line of fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F2</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of the additional\nfuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98A</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ; a reference voltage is received from pin 88 of \n\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              . It is supplied by the control unit from pin 97 of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ,\nand sends to pin 89 a signal proportional to the air flow. K41 also\ncontains an air temperature sensor which sends an air temperature\nsignal to pin 86 of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>Accelerator pedal K55 is fitted with two\nbuilt-in potentiometers (a main one and a safety back-up). The first\nreceives power and earth from pins 78 and 76 respectively of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and\nsends a corresponding signal to pin 77. The second receives power\nand earth from pins 81 and 79 respectively of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and sends a\nsignal to pin 80.</p><p>Fuel temperature sensor \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K81</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               fitted\non the return manifold measures the temperature of diesel leaving\nthe injectors. It receives a reference earth from pin 83 of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and\nsends the fuel temperature signal to pin 82.</p><p>The supercharging sensor \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K82</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               measures\nthe turbocharger pressure. It is supplied by pin 93 of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and\nreceives a reference earth from pin 95. The signal is sent to in\n94 of the control unit.</p><p>The fuel pressure sensor \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K83</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is responsible\nfor providing the injection control unit with a feedback signal\nfor governing pressure and injection duration. It receives the power\nand reference earth from pins 90 and 92 of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ; it then sends\nthe pressure signal to pin 91.</p><p>The fuel pressure regulator \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N77</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               has\nthe task of keeping the value of the fuel pressure in the accumulator\nconstant. The two control signals come from pins 108 and 109 of\nthe control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The EGR solenoid \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>L30</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               controls exhaust\ngas recirculation. It is supplied from the line of fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F2</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of\nthe additional fuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98A</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and is controlled by a signal of\npin 16 of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The turbine variable geometry control solenoid \n\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>L36</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               governs the operation of the turbine in accordance with\nengine load; it is supplied by the line of fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F2</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of the\nadditional fuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98A</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and is controlled by a signal from\npin 17 of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The solenoid valve on the throttle casing \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>L62\nshutters and closes the throttle, for example when the engine is\nswitched off;</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               it is supplied by the line of fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F2</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of\nthe additional fuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98A</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              and is controlled by a signal of\npin 15 of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>Pin 59 of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10 receives the signal coming\nfrom the brake lights switch I30, with the supply controlled by\nthe ignition (INT) from fuse F1 of the junction unit B1, or, depending\non the version, from fuse F4 of the additional fuse box B98 B.</strong></p><p>Pin 62 of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               receives an earth signal\ncoming from the clutch pedal switch \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>l31</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The injectors \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N70</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               receive the opening\ngo ahead supply from pins 117 (cylinders 1 and 2) and 118 (cylinders\n3 and 4) of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The engine control unit sends commands to\nthe injectors \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N70</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               from pins 119, 120, 121 and 114 of connector\nA for cylinders 1, 2, 3 and 4, respectively.</p><p>Control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10 - pins 10 and 9 - communicates\nwith ABS control unit  M50 via the CAN line: this line, on versions\nwith VDC, passes through steering sensor K58 and reaches ABS control\nunit M50.</strong></p><p>The rev counter module \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E15 receives a\nsupply controlled by the ignition (INT) from the line protected\nby fuse F4 of the additional fuse box B98B; when the earth signal\narrives from pin 21 of M10, the &#x27;injection failure&#x27; warning light\ncomes on (starting from September 2003, EOBD warning light).</strong></p><p>The rev counter  module \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E15 also receives\na supply controlled by the ignition (INT) from the line protected\nby fuse F4 of the additional fuse box B98B; when the earth signal\narrives from pin 14 of M10, the &#x27;heater plugs&#x27; warning light comes\non.</strong></p><p>The coolant temperature signal is sent to\nthe auxiliary instrument from pin 110 of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong><a href=\"#/3234358\">E4023</a>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is connected\nto the ALFA ROMEO CODE control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M20</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               via a specific line\nfrom pin 11; in this way if the ALFA ROMEO CODE unit does not detect\na correct code, it does not issue enablement and the engine is not\nstarted.</p><p>The control unit is equipped with a self-diagnostic\nunit that may be used by connecting the unit to connector \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>R10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               via\npin 48.</p><p>The control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               sends a signal\nfrom pin 47 proportional to the engine speed \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <a href=\"#/3234270\">E4020</a>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is connected\nto the air conditioning system through pins 18 and 60. This makes\nit possible to adjust the engine idle speed as the load increases\neach time the compressor is switched on or to switch off the compressor\nin the case of high engine speed or load conditions \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <a href=\"#/3234652\">E6021</a>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The control unit also controls the engine\ncooling system: pins 19, 20, 51 and 52 control the engagement of\nthe relevant fans \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <a href=\"#/3234439\">E5020</a>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>Cruise Control management signals leave\npins 23, 53, 54, 55, 56 and 57 of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10\n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 See\n\t\tE5060\n\t\tCRUISE CONTROL\n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 .</strong></p>"]]